  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the Concept**\n\nI\'m solidifying the core concept: a mobile-first web app, adaptable to full-screen, focused on historical markers and driving alerts. \"Historical Marker Explorer & Driving Alert System\" feels a bit clunky, so I\'m considering alternatives like \"HistDrive.\" I\'m prioritizing responsiveness and mobile optimization as fundamental design principles.\n\n\n**Analyzing Feature Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously breaking down the user\'s feature requests. I need to nail down the core functionalities. GPS proximity alerts while driving, including the text-to-speech feature, photo display, and user toggles, are all essential. The map view with historical point filtering is also critical. Now I\'m carefully considering how to integrate these elements seamlessly within the mobile-first design.\n\n\n**Defining Route and Simulation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on route planning features: users should select routes (point-to-point or multi-stop scenic) and have all relevant markers highlighted within a buffer. Crucially, I\'m integrating a \"Drive Simulation\" mode for testing, enabling simulated GPS movement with triggering TTS alerts and marker popups, crucial for user feedback! I think this will greatly enhance testing and demonstration capabilities.\n\n\n**Evaluating Skill Relevance**\n\nI\'ve just done a crucial skill check and re-assessed available tools. I see that `gemini-api`, `google-maps-platform`, and `image-generation` are directly relevant to building out rich historical details, location data, map rendering, and imagery to enhance the driving and marker experience. This will allow the application to provide rich, engaging historical content.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 766605213
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
