  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining App Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on defining the user\'s mobile app requirements. I\'m focusing on the core functionalities: GPS-based alerts for historical markers, text-to-speech for the marker\'s text, and providing accompanying photos. This also includes defining platforms: Android and Apple.\n\n\n**Developing Drive Mode Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the drive mode features. This encompasses real-time GPS tracking and an interactive drive simulator. I\'m focusing on allowing users to select routes, set custom speeds, and view real-time data like speed, heading, and distance to the next marker. I want a map view to show historical points of interest along the chosen route. Also, I\'m integrating a mobile-feeling view for both iOS and Android.\n\n\n**Refining Discovery & Triggers**\n\nI am now building out the historical markers database and the real-time discovery features. I\'m focusing on an interactive map with markers spanning historical routes, including the ability to filter by era and category. Also, I\'m integrating proximity triggers and auto-announce/auto-show toggles, including alert radius and speech settings.\n\n\n**Expanding Site Detail**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on enriching the user\'s experience. This includes implementing a photo gallery for each site, high-resolution marker photos, and integration of AI Storyteller/Plaque Expander using the Gemini API for more in-depth historical context. I am also implementing marker text with an attractive bronze / cast-iron plaque styling with vintage typography.\n\n**Planning Route Details**\n\nI am now focusing on providing a well-defined tour with route-based features. Users can now choose origin and destination points, and I can calculate the route polyline and identify historical markers along the chosen route. I\'m focusing on displaying this list in order: Marker 1 -> Marker 2 -> Marker 3, with along-route distance, estimated time of arrival, and voice touring.\n\n\n**Implementing Audio Controls**\n\nNow I\'m designing the audio player for the app. The key features I am working on are the in-app playback controls: play/pause, stop, replay, adjustable speech rate, voice selection, mute, and a current reading highlight. Furthermore, I am assessing the need for an Express backend for the app. This will be integrated with the Vite build process.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 668779942
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
