  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Current Build**\n\nI\'m checking the mobile app framing implementation for iOS and Android, ensuring the frame switcher (iPhone, Android, Fullscreen) functions as expected. I\'m also reviewing the GPS proximity alert functionality, specifically focusing on its accuracy with both real location data and the interactive simulation mode.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built **HistoriDrive**, a mobile application designed for smartphone viewports (with iPhone, Android, and Fullscreen preview modes) that alerts drivers to upcoming historical markers using GPS location data, reads plaque inscriptions via text-to-speech, and displays site photography and historical deep-dives upon arrival.\n\n### Key Features Implemented:\n\n- **GPS Proximity Driving Alert System**:\n  - **Live GPS Tracking**: Uses `navigator.geolocation.watchPosition` for real-time driving.\n  - **Drive Simulator Mode**: Allows users to simulate driving along scenic highway routes (at 30\342\200\22370 MPH) to test proximity triggers, speedometers, and auto-announcements directly from their browser.\n  - **Proximity Radar HUD**: Real-time distance countdown to the next marker along the route with progress bars.\n\n- **User Preference Toggles**:\n  - **Auto-Announce Speech**: Toggle automatic text-to-speech narration when entering marker proximity.\n  - **Auto-Show Plaque**: Toggle automatic popup display of site photos and plaque details on arrival.\n  - **Proximity Distance Threshold**: Adjust alert radius between `250m` (~0.15 mi), `500m` (~0.3 mi), and `1000m` (~0.6 mi).\n  - **Voice & Speed Controls**: Customize text-to-speech voice selection, speech rate (`0.8x` to `1.5x`), and pitch.\n\n- **Plaque View & Site Photography**:\n  - **Embossed Bronze Plaque Rendering**: Authentically styled metallic bronze/cast-iron plaque display with marker ID numbers and official state commission formatting.\n  - **Interactive Word Highlighter**: Highlights words in real-time on the plaque text as the text-to-speech engine reads them aloud.\n  - **Photo Gallery**: High-resolution photography of the site, monuments, and plaques.\n  - **AI Audio Storyteller**: Server-side Gemini API integration (`/api/marker-story`) that generates deep-dive audio narratives, key historical figures, and oral legends expanding beyond the physical plaque text.\n\n- **Interactive Map & Category Explorer**:\n  - OpenStreetMap dark-mode tiles with custom bronze shield pins.\n  - Filter markers by era and category (*Revolutionary War, Civil War, Pioneer Trails, Architecture, Indigenous Heritage, Music & Culture, Aviation & Transit, Science & Industry, Notable Figures*).\n\n- **Route Choice & Corridor Marker Finder**:\n  - **Preset Scenic Driving Routes**: Includes famous routes such as the *Paul Revere & Minuteman Trail (Route 2)*, *Route 66 Heritage Highway*, *Blue Ridge Parkway*, *Pacific Coast Highway 1*, and *Colonial Potomac Highway*.\n  - **Corridor Marker Identification**: Computes all historical markers along the chosen route corridor within a configurable buffer (1 to 5 miles) ordered chronologically with arrival ETAs."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 309678417
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
