  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing TTS Errors**\n\nI\'m currently investigating the root causes of the \"TTS utterance error\" that appears in `useTTS.ts`, particularly focusing on the `onerror` event of `SpeechSynthesisUtterance`. The Web Speech API\'s nuances are proving tricky. It looks like an unscheduled `speechSynthesis.cancel()` call, for instance, in Chrome/Blink browsers, might immediately trigger this error. I\'m focusing on debugging that possibility.\n\n\n**Clarifying Error Conditions**\n\nI\'ve clarified the error conditions associated with TTS interruptions. Notably, \'canceled\' and \'interrupted\' errors, as reported in `utterance.onerror`, aren\'t failures but expected lifecycle events. This often happens when speech is preempted by user actions or changes in settings, for instance. I\'m taking into account how the `voices` state in `useTTS.ts` affects voice assignment within the `speak` function. I am also investigating the impact of initial user interaction requirements in Chrome.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 954095075
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
