ng on ensuring a robust fallback mechanism to prevent these issues. I will prioritize a suitable default voice selection when the preferred voice cannot be found.\n\n\n**Implementing Voice Fallback**\n\nI\'ve implemented a more robust voice selection fallback. If the user\'s preferred voice isn\'t available, I now prioritize English voices, and then a default voice to prevent \"synthesis-failed\" errors.\n\nI\'m checking `speechSynthesis.resume()` / `speak()` issue in Chrome. Sometimes `cancel()` needs a brief microtask or clean to prevent chrome issue.\n\n\n"
