  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Data Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `server.ts` and the React frontend share data. I\'ve noted that `HISTORICAL_MARKERS` and `PRESET_ROUTES` from `markersData.js` are critical for both the backend and frontend. I\'m drilling down into the specific uses of each data point across these two separate systems.\n\n\n**Refining Geographic Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on restricting all data within `markersData.ts` to Missouri. This means every marker\'s state property will be \'MO\', and routes must originate, terminate, or traverse the state. The default route and initial state in `App.tsx` and all initial saved states will be updated to reflect Missouri-centric markers and routes. Additionally, I\'ll update the hardcoded default saved marker and then confirm marker authenticity.\n\n\n**Compiling Marker Details**\n\nI\'m now compiling a list of rich Missouri historical markers, focusing on famous and historic locations. I\'m gathering details like coordinates, plaque texts, categories, eras, and photos for markers like the Gateway Arch, the Historic Chain of Rocks Bridge, Meramec Caverns, the 66 Drive-In Theatre, and Mark Twain\'s Boyhood Home. I\'m also planning Missouri driving routes that include these markers.\n\n\n**Listing Historical Markers**\n\nI\'ve added several more rich historical markers to the list, detailing locations such as the Mark Twain Birthplace, the Pony Express National Museum & Stables, the Harry S. Truman National Historic Site, Wilson\'s Creek National Battlefield, and the Ste. Genevieve Historic District. I\'m noting each marker\'s category, era, coordinates, and associated driving route. This expanded list helps to enrich the Missouri-centric context.\n\n\n**Expanding Marker Catalog**\n\nI\'ve added key historical markers, including the \"Iron Curtain\" Speech site, Union Station in Kansas City, Ted Drewes, and the Old Courthouse, noting their era, category, coordinates and driving route. I\'m now developing a set of preset driving routes across Missouri. I\'ve begun to list the waypoints and significant markers for Route 66 in Missouri.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 310197578
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
