  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Initial Coordinates**\n\nI\'ve updated the default `mapCenter` in `MapView.tsx` to St. Louis, Missouri. The previous default was Boston, now it\'s `[38.6247, -90.1848]` to center on the Gateway Arch. I also need to check the `CATEGORIES` array within the same file for appropriate historical event categories.\n\n\n**Listing Missouri Markers**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating a comprehensive list of Missouri markers and scenic routes for `markersData.ts`. I\'ve begun to list approximately 12-15 rich Missouri markers, including the Gateway Arch. I also plan to add 4-5 scenic driving routes across Missouri to ensure complete geographic representation. I\'m carefully constructing the initial marker entries, including title, subtitle, plaque text, and appropriate categories like \'Frontier & Pioneer\' or \'Architecture\'.\n\n\n**Adding New Markers**\n\nI\'ve just added a new Missouri marker entry for the Gateway Arch, documenting its historical context as the departure point for Lewis and Clark. I\'ve included relevant data such as its era (1803 / 1965), geographic coordinates, city and state, year erected, marker number, route IDs, and historical context. I\'ve also added a marker for the Historic Chain of Rocks Bridge, including its title, subtitle, plaque text, category, and precise coordinates, and year erected.\n\n\n**Expanding Missouri Markers**\n\nI\'ve just added a new marker for the Old Courthouse and the Dred Scott Trial Site. I\'ve input essential details like title, subtitle, plaque text, category, coordinates, year erected, and historical context. I\'m focusing on providing rich historical context for each marker, including the impact of the Dred Scott decision. I\'ve also added the RouteIds for the marker. This entry is now complete.\n\n\n**Adding Historical Markers**\n\nI\'ve just added a new Missouri marker: Meramec Caverns, including details on its Jesse James connection, geographic coordinates, and historical context as a Route 66 attraction. I\'ve also detailed the National Churchill Museum and the Iron Curtain location at Westminster College, marking the geopolitical significance of the site, plus geographic coordinates. I\'m focusing on ensuring these entries are rich in historical detail.\n\n\n**Adding New Missouri Markers**\n\nI\'ve just added a new Missouri marker: the National Churchill Museum at Westminster College. I\'ve documented its significance with Winston Churchill\'s \"Sinews of Peace\" address, including plaque text that captures the essence of the \"Iron Curtain\" speech, and noting the dismantled London church. I\'ve also added the Mark Twain Boyhood Home & Historic District marker, including all essential details. I\'m focusing on ensuring these entries are rich in historical detail.\n\n\n**Adding Twain & Express**\n\nI\'ve just added the Mark Twain marker in Hannibal, documenting his connection to the Mississippi River, its bluffs, and their influence on his work. I\'ve also added the Pony Express National Museum & Pikes Peak Stables marker, detailing its historical importance as the starting point for the Pony Express mail service, with full details included.\n\n\n**Adding New Markers**\n\nI\'ve just added a new marker for the Pony Express National Museum in St. Joseph. This new entry includes latitude and longitude, city and state, year erected, marker number, route IDs, and historical context. The details are set to reflect riders changing horses every 10-15 miles in rugged terrain. Additionally, I\'ve just documented the home of the 33rd President with the Harry S. Truman National Historic Site marker.\n\n\n\n**Adding Truman and Union**\n\nI\'ve just added the Harry S. Truman National Historic Site marker with a focus on his daily walks. I also just documented Union Station Kansas City, and the Kansas City Massacre. I have detailed its Beaux-Arts architecture, historical context as a rail hub, the infamous shootout, and its architectural significance.\n\n\n**Adding Civil War Details**\n\nI\'ve just added Wilson\'s Creek National Battlefield, detailing the first major Civil War engagement west of the Mississippi, including General Lyon\'s death. I\'ve included the plaque text, coordinates, era, and route IDs. I\'ve also detailed the Historic 66 Drive-In Theatre, with an opening date and location. I am now working on further markers.\n\n\n**Documenting Mother Road Theatre**\n\nI\'ve just added the Historic 66 Drive-In Theatre in Carthage, focusing on its cultural significance, original neon sign, and steel screen. The entry includes its opening date, category, era, geographic coordinates, and historical context as evening entertainment during Route 66\'s peak. I\'ve also detailed the Ste. Genevieve Historic French Colonial District, noting its founding in 1735 and its preservation of French Colonial architecture.\n\n\n**Adding Colonial District and Concretes**\n\nI\'ve just added the Ste. Genevieve Historic French Colonial District marker, including its founding details, coordinates, year erected, and Route IDs. The historical context focuses on original structures like the Bolduc House and Beauvais-Amoureux House. I\'ve also detailed Ted Drewes Frozen Custard - Route 66, marking its significance as a St. Louis landmark and Route 66 pit-stop with the famous \"concrete\" milkshakes. I\'ve now included its opening year, motto, and precise geographic data.\n\n\n**Adding Hermann and Route 66**\n\nI\'ve just added a new Missouri marker for the Hermann Historic German Wine Country, including its historical context, coordinates, and details of its founding in 1837. I\'ve also detailed its historical context as a significant wine-producing region. I\'m now adding a Missouri driving route, \"Route 66 Missouri Mother Road Byway,\" including a description and important locations.\n\n\n**Defining Route Parameters**\n\nI\'ve just defined the driving route, \"Chain of Rocks to 66 Drive-In,\" focusing on a St. Louis to Carthage tour. I\'ve set up its main features, including a `coverPhoto` image from Unsplash. I\'ve specified a `distanceMiles` of approximately 290 miles, with a 4.5-hour driving time. I\'ve also added the start and end points and created waypoints for key locations along the route, including Chain of Rocks Bridge, the Gateway Arch, Ted Drewes, Meramec Caverns, Wilson\'s Creek, and 66 Drive-In.\n\n\n**Defining River Route**\n\nI\'ve just added a new Missouri driving route: \"Great River Road Missouri (MO Hwy 61)\". This new entry details a journey along the Mississippi River, including its name, subtitle, and description. I\'ve also set approximate driving time and distance. I\'ve focused on essential waypoints for a complete Missouri experience, from Hannibal to Ste. Genevieve. I\'m carefully constructing this entry to ensure complete detail.\n\n\n**Expanding Route Information**\n\nI\'ve just added route details for the \"Missouri Pioneer & Overland Express Highway\". I\'ve included a description of the scenic drive from St. Joseph to Kansas City, including its historical significance related to the Pony Express. I\'ve included the cover photo from Unsplash and the approximate distance and driving time, plus waypoints. I am now working on expanding the route\'s historical detail.\n\n\n**Adding Route Detail**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Missouri Pioneer & Overland Express Highway\". I have focused on new details for the \"Missouri River Heritage Corridor (I-70 / US-54)\" route, focusing on its waypoints. I\'ve documented the Pony Express, Union Station KC, and Truman\'s home with their coordinates. I have a detailed description of the route and its significant points.\n\n\n**Updating Route Waypoints**\n\nI\'m currently updating the \"Missouri River Heritage Corridor\" route with precise waypoints. I have finalized the start and end points in `markersData.ts`, including the bounds. The waypoints are: Kansas City Union Station, Truman Home, Churchill Museum Fulton, Hermann German Wineries, and the Gateway Arch. I also updated the markerIds to ensure route consistency. My next step will be testing this route.\n\n\n"
