          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Standing 630 feet tall on the west bank of the Mississippi River in St. Louis, the Gateway Arch commemorates Thomas Jefferson\\\'s Louisiana Purchase of 1803 and the westward expansion of the United States. Designed by architect Eero Saarinen in 1947 and completed in 1965, it remains the tallest national monument in the Western Hemisphere.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
