    modified_response: "You do **not** need to copy and paste code into Android Studio to run or test your application! \n\nYour app is built as a responsive web application that runs directly in any web browser (on desktop, Android phones, iPhones, tablets, etc.). Here are the options for deploying, sharing, or downloading your project:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Accessing & Testing the Live App**\n- Your app is already live and running in your browser!\n- You can test it directly on your mobile device by opening the share link:\n  **[View Live Application](https://ais-pre-ffp54kytccfgtbn5an55dx-637039075391.us-west2.run.app)**\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Deploying & Sharing from AI Studio**\n- **Share Link:** Click the **Share** button in the top-right header of Google AI Studio to generate a link you can open on your phone or send to others.\n- **Deploy to Cloud Run:** You can deploy the app to production directly through the AI Studio interface.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Exporting Source Code**\nIf you want to save the code to your computer or work on it locally in VS Code:\n- Click the **Settings** / **Export** menu in AI Studio.\n- Choose **Export to GitHub** or **Download as ZIP**.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Running on an Android Device**\n- **Web / Progressive App (Easiest):** Open the shared web link in Google Chrome on your Android phone, tap the three dots menu, and select **\"Add to Home Screen\"**. It will install and launch just like a native Android app.\n- **Native Android App (.apk):** If you specifically want to generate an `.apk` file for the Google Play Store, you can export the codebase to your computer and use a tool like **Capacitor** (`npx cap add android`) or **Cordova** to wrap the React web app into a native Android Studio project."
