  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the 404 Issue**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a plan to troubleshoot the 404 error users are experiencing in mobile Chrome. My current direction involves outlining clear, step-by-step guidance for them. I will outline how users can share and open the application on mobile.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Share Process**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Share\" functionality within AI Studio. The key is understanding the distinction between the \"Shared App URL\" (accessible to all) and the \"Development preview URL\" (private). I see that incomplete URLs or those typed manually are leading to 404s. The HTTPS requirement on mobile browsers, as opposed to HTTP, is a key concern and common mistake to consider. I\'m focusing on user-friendly instructions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "A 404 error on your phone usually happens because mobile Chrome is trying to access either a truncated link or the private development container URL instead of the public preview link.\n\n### \360\237\224\227 Your Live Application Link\n\nHere is your direct application link:\n\n\360\237\221\211 **[https://ais-pre-ffp54kytccfgtbn5an55dx-637039075391.us-west2.run.app](https://ais-pre-ffp54kytccfgtbn5an55dx-637039075391.us-west2.run.app)**\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\261 How to Properly Share & Open the App on Mobile\n\n1. **Use the \"Share\" Button**: In the upper-right corner of the **Google AI Studio** workspace, click the **Share** button.\n2. **Copy the Link**: Select **Copy Link**. This link is specifically formatted for public viewing on any mobile or desktop web browser.\n3. **Open in Mobile Chrome**:\n   - Paste the link into Mobile Chrome.\n   - Ensure the link starts with `https://` (not `http://`).\n\n---\n\n### \342\232\240\357\270\217 Common Causes for 404 Errors\n\n* **Private Development URL vs. Shared URL**: The development URL (`ais-dev-...`) is tied to your active editing session. On mobile devices without an active session login, it returns a 404 or access denied error. Use the **Shared URL** (`ais-pre-...`) linked above instead.\n* **Manual Typing Errors**: The long alphanumeric address is easy to mistype. Copying and pasting or scanning a QR code prevents missed characters.\n* **`localhost` or Local IP**: Typing `localhost:3000` on a phone attempts to load a server on the phone itself rather than the Cloud container."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 885383484
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
